# VTID-03808 — commands run

## 1. Allocate the VTID (before touching code, per §4.1)

curl -s -X POST "https://gateway.vitanaland.com/api/v1/vtid/allocate" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"source":"claude-code","layer":"frontend","module":"orb-widget"}'
# -> {"ok":true,"vtid":"VTID-03808","num":3808,...}
# then UPDATE vtid_ledger SET title=..., status='in_progress', spec_status='approved'

## 2. Rule out the obvious before hunting

grep -n "_userRequestedClose|closeBtn|onClose" orb-widget.js
# -> closeBtn.addEventListener('click', _hide) — unconditional, never disabled
grep -n "pointerEvents|\.disabled\s*=|opacity" orb-widget.js
# -> only the auras, already pointer-events:none (they cannot intercept)
sed -n '4596,4700p' orb-widget.js
# -> _hide() is fully try/catch'd and stops audio synchronously (VTID-03295)
# Conclusion: the handler is fine. Nothing reaches it.

## 3. Find what is actually swallowing the tap

# The overlay is appended to document.body, outside React. What is on body?
grep -n "activateOrb|setOpenTopic" vitana-v1/src/components/journey/GuidedJourneyCatalog.tsx
# -> 260: activateOrb(topic.topicId)   then   269: setOpenTopic(topic)
# -> 279: activateOrb(firstTopic...)   then   283: setOpenTopic(firstTopic)
#    i.e. a drawer is opened right behind the ORB and stays open all lesson

grep -n "Drawer|modal" vitana-v1/src/components/ui/drawer.tsx
# -> vaul DrawerPrimitive.Root — modal by DEFAULT

python3 -c "read react-remove-scroll/dist/es2015/SideEffect.js around 'pointer-events'"
# -> .block-interactivity-<id> { pointer-events: none; }   applied to document.body
#    .allow-interactivity-<id> { pointer-events: all;  }   applied to the drawer only
# The widget root is in the blocked subtree and outside the allowed one.

## 4. Prove it in a real browser (jsdom cannot hit-test pointer-events)

node docs/validation/VTID-03808/outputs/pointer-events-hit-test.probe.mjs
# BEFORE: computed=none, elementFromPoint at the X's centre = HTML, handler ran = false
# AFTER : computed=auto, elementFromPoint at the X's centre = close, handler ran = true
# VERDICT: reproduces the report AND confirms the fix

